    "narrative": "For the May 14th slate, the **Austin Waves** offense is anchored by **Kyle Tucker**, whose 66.99 efficiency score makes him our clear start of the day. Facing Landen Roupp (4.07 xERA), **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-floor matchup, receiving a boost from his projected #5 spot in the order. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (58.63) also presents a strong play against Chayce Burns, the case for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is particularly bolstered by favorable wind conditions and a significant dynamic platoon advantage, which helps mitigate the threat of a pitcher with a 3.01 xERA. **Andy Pages** (57.86) also projects well, maintaining value against Roupp despite the marginal suppression of his efficiency score caused by the opposing battery's elite pop time.\n\nThe lineup architecture hinges on mitigating tough matchups against Chayce Burns, who creates a challenging environment for **Nasim Nunez** (44.16) and **Brady House** (47.12). These players remain in the starting rotation primarily due to the scarcity of stolen base threats, a core tenet of our 5x5 strategy. **Miguel Vargas** (52.68) serves as our most reliable utility option, buoyed by a platoon-advantage matchup against Kris Bubic. Looking at the bench, **Dominic Smith** (41.72) was the closest to a demotion; he remains in the lineup solely because his platoon split marginally outperformed alternative bench depth, but he sits near the bottom of our efficiency threshold. We are monitoring the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, as his absence continues to force us to rely on higher-volume, lower-efficiency depth pieces like **Dominic Smith** and **Drake Baldwin** to maintain our game-cap targets.\n\nInvestors should note that we are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions for several slots, including **Drake Baldwin**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Dominic Smith**, **Andy Pages**, and **Miguel Vargas**. Should any of these players drop in the order or be sidelined for rest, their efficiency scores will crater, necessitating an immediate pivot to our available bench depth. We continue to hold **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** in reserve due to today's schedule gap, while **Jackson Merrill** remains sidelined. We are closely watching the development of **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Nolan Schanuel** to ensure our roster depth remains optimized for long-term category growth.",
